{"siman":520,"seifim":[1],"sourceMeta":[{"slug":"ateret-zekenim","title":"Ateret Zekeinim","dataKey":"ateret_zekenim"},{"slug":"baer-heitev","title":"Baer Hetev","dataKey":"baer_heitev"},{"slug":"beer-hagolah","title":"Be'er HaGolah","dataKey":"beer_hagolah"},{"slug":"beur-hagra","title":"Biur HaGRA","dataKey":"beur_hagra"},{"slug":"biur-halacha","title":"Biur Halacha","dataKey":"biur_halacha"},{"slug":"chatam-sofer","title":"Chatam Sofer","dataKey":"chatam_sofer"},{"slug":"chokhmat-shlomo","title":"Chokhmat Shlomo","dataKey":"chokhmat_shlomo"},{"slug":"dagul-merevavah","title":"Dagul Merevavah","dataKey":"dagul_merevavah"},{"slug":"eliyah-rabbah","title":"Eliyah Rabbah","dataKey":"eliyah_rabbah"},{"slug":"eshel-avraham","title":"Eshel Avraham","dataKey":"eshel_avraham"},{"slug":"kaf-hachayim","title":"Kaf HaChayyim","dataKey":"kaf_hachayim"},{"slug":"levushei-serad","title":"Levushei Serad","dataKey":"levushei_serad"},{"slug":"machatzit-hashekel","title":"Machatzit HaShekel","dataKey":"machatzit_hashekel"},{"slug":"magen-avraham","title":"Magen Avraham","dataKey":"magen_avraham"},{"slug":"mishnah-berurah","title":"Mishnah Berurah","dataKey":"mishnah_berurah"},{"slug":"netiv-chayim","title":"Netiv Chayim","dataKey":"netiv_chayim"},{"slug":"peri-megadim","title":"Pri Megadim","dataKey":"peri_megadim"},{"slug":"rabbi-akiva-eiger","title":"Rabbi Akiva Eiger","dataKey":"rabbi_akiva_eiger"},{"slug":"shaarei-teshuvah","title":"Shaarei Teshuvah","dataKey":"shaarei_teshuvah"},{"slug":"turei-zahav","title":"Turei Zahav (Taz)","dataKey":"turei_zahav"},{"slug":"yad-ephraim","title":"Yad Ephraim","dataKey":"yad_ephraim"}],"data":{"1":{"mechaber":{"he":"<b>לכבד הבית. ובו סעיף אחד:</b><br><i data-commentator=\"Be'er HaGolah\" data-label=\"א\" data-order=\"1\"></i>לכבד הבי' כדינו בשב' כך דינו בי\"ט: <small>[<i data-commentator=\"Mishnah Berurah\" data-label=\"א\"></i>וע' לעיל סי' של\"ז]</small>:","en":"<b>Sweeping the House, One Siman: The law of sweeping the house is</b><br> <i data-commentator=\"Be'er HaGolah\" data-label=\"א\" data-order=\"1\"></i> the same on a holiday as it is on Shabbat (and see above chapter 337).<small>[<i data-commentator=\"Mishnah Berurah\" data-label=\"א\"></i>]</small>:"},"beer_hagolah":{"he":"ציינתיו לעיל סי' של\"ו","en":"I noted it above in siman 336."},"beur_hagra":{"he":"<b>ס\"א לכבד כו'. </b>שם כ\"ב ב':","en":"I am honored as a. Named \"B\":"},"eliyah_rabbah":{"he":"[א] <b>לכבד וכו'.</b> וכל סימן זה נתבאר בסימן של\"ז:","en":"<b>To sweep, etc.</b> And this entire siman is elucidated in siman 337."},"kaf_hachayim":{"he":"","en":""},"mishnah_berurah":{"he":"{א} וע\"ל סימן של\"ז - שם מבואר הדין אם הקרקע היה מרוצף ושאר פרטים:","en":"And see above, siman 337: there the law is clarified whether the ground was paved, and the other details."},"_included":["beer_hagolah","beur_hagra","eliyah_rabbah","kaf_hachayim","mishnah_berurah"]}}}